<Page title="Bring us a real workflow." description="Request an AI Assurance assessment when you need evidence for a deployment, model selection or improvement decision. Start with a high-level description of the work, the target system and the failures that matter. Vorbtech will review fit and agree scope, access and terms before testing begins." eyebrow="Assessment requests"><h2>What should I prepare?</h2><ol><li><strong>Workflow:</strong> Who uses it, what it does and the outcome you need.</li><li><strong>Target system:</strong> Model, provider, architecture and relevant configuration.</li><li><strong>Rules:</strong> Approval limits, escalation, allowed sources, tool authority and data handling.</li><li><strong>Risks:</strong> The failures with the greatest practical consequence.</li><li><strong>Data and access:</strong> Available synthetic data, fixtures or sandbox access you are authorised to share.</li><li><strong>Success criteria:</strong> Requirements, thresholds and internal decision criteria.</li><li><strong>Stakeholders:</strong> Technical, operations, security, privacy, legal and domain reviewers.</li><li><strong>Timing and constraints:</strong> Deadline, prohibited actions, budget and procurement needs.</li></ol><div class="ak-note"><strong>The GitHub request is public.</strong> Share a high-level summary only. Do not submit credentials, personal data, production records or proprietary documents. A suitable private channel must be agreed before sensitive scoping.</div><div class="ak-actions"><a class="ak-btn" href="https://github.com/code-sensei/artemiskit/issues/new?title=AI%20Assurance%20assessment%20request">Open a public request ↗</a><a class="ak-btn outline" href="https://github.com/code-sensei/artemiskit/blob/main/AI_ASSURANCE.md">Read the assessment brief ↗</a></div><h2>What happens next?</h2><p>We review fit, identify a private channel for confidential scoping, and agree boundaries, data handling, timing and commercial terms. Submitting a request does not create an engagement or authorise testing.</p></Page>
